invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_square returns without wiping d, twice its operand,
  so after every square a signature makes the dead frame holds the
  power it squared, shifted up one bit. No output changes, so no vector
  notices. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below a signature
  and finds two words of a value the signature held.

--- old
    ct_wipe(d, (k + 1) * sizeof(uint64_t));
    ct_wipe(t, (k + 2) * sizeof(uint64_t));
--- new
    ct_wipe(t, (k + 2) * sizeof(uint64_t));
